{{> head}}

    <style>
        h6 {
            font-size: .9rem;
            font-weight: 600;
        }
        #agreement {
            max-height: 70vh;
            overflow-y: scroll;
            border-radius: 5px;
            font-size: .75em;
        }
    </style>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-center align-items-lg-center full-height-fix">

        <div class="card text-center" id="apl-card" style="display: none;">
            <div class="card-body pt-4">
                <h5 class="card-title text-info mb-0">Professional Driver Application</h5>
                <p class="text-secondary fs-6 fw-light mb-1"><small>Powered by {{siteName}} <sup style="font-size: 62%;">TM</sup></small></p>
                <section class="border text-start py-3 px-2" id="agreement">
                    <h6>Applicant Certification and Authorization Statement</h6>
                    <div>
                        <p class="my-2">
                            By submitting this application, I certify that I have personally completed it and that all information provided is true and accurate to the best of my knowledge.
                            I authorize the company, its agents, or contractors who receive this application to conduct, at any time, an investigation of my background for employment purposes.
                            This investigation may include, but is not limited to, information regarding my character, general reputation, personal characteristics, lifestyle, criminal history, driving record, credit history, employment history, education, alcohol or drug test results (including any refusal to test), or any other relevant information.
                            This information may be obtained from individuals, organizations, entities, agencies, or other sources with knowledge of such matters.
                        </p>
                        <p class="my-2">
                            If I am hired or contracted, this authorization shall remain on file and shall serve as ongoing authorization for the company to obtain consumer reports at any time during my employment or contract term.
                            I have completed this application voluntarily and release the employer, its agents, and contractors from any liability related to providing this application for my use.
                        </p>
                        <p class="my-2">
                            I consent to receiving text (SMS) messages from the employer and/or its affiliates regarding my application for employment.
                            I have read and understand the job description and certify that I am capable of meeting its requirements.
                            I understand that I may be contacted by email, phone, or direct mail.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <h6 class="mt-3">Employee Consent Form</h6>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        I certify that the answers provided in this application are true and complete to the best of my knowledge.
                        I authorize investigation of all statements contained in this application, including records such as Motor Vehicle Reports and references, as may be necessary for the employer to make an employment decision.
                    </p>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        I understand and acknowledge that, unless otherwise governed by applicable law, my employment with this organization is at will — meaning that either I or the employer may terminate the relationship at any time, with or without cause.
                        I also understand that no document or conduct shall alter this at-will relationship unless acknowledged in writing by an authorized executive of the organization.
                    </p>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        In the event of employment, I understand that any false or misleading information provided in this application or during interviews may result in discharge. I agree to abide by all rules and policies of the employer.
                    </p>
                    <h6 class="mt-3">Employee Consent Form</h6>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        In accordance with Section 604(b)(2)(A) of the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA), Public Law 91-508, as amended by the Consumer Credit Reporting Act of 1996, you are hereby informed that reports verifying your employment history, drug and alcohol test results, and driving record may be obtained for employment purposes.
                        These reports are required under Sections 382.413, 391.23, and 391.25 of the Federal Motor Carrier Safety Regulations.
                    </p>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        I authorize the release of my DOT-regulated drug and alcohol testing records by my previous employers (as listed in Section I-B) to the employer listed in Section I-A.
                        This release complies with DOT Regulation 49 CFR Part 40, Section 40.25. The information may include:
                        <ol>
                            <li>Alcohol tests with results of 0.04 or higher;</li>
                            <li>Verified positive drug test results;</li>
                            <li>Refusals to be tested;</li>
                            <li>Other violations of DOT drug and alcohol testing regulations;</li>
                            <li>Reports of drug and alcohol rule violations from prior employers;</li>
                            <li>Documentation, if any, of completion of the return-to-duty process.</li>
                        </ol>
                    </p>
                    <h6 class="mt-3 mb-1">Request and Consent for Information from Previous Employer(s)</h6>
                    <h6><small>Including Alcohol/Controlled Substances Testing and Employment Records (FMCSA Disclosure and Release)</small></h6>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        Pursuant to DOT Regulation 49 CFR Part 391.23, I authorize the carriers (companies or schools) listed above to release DOT-regulated drug and alcohol testing records to “Carrier”, or to HireRight and DriverFacts solely for the purpose of transmitting these records.
                    </p>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        I authorize the release of the following items from the past three years:
                        <ul>
                            <li>Alcohol tests with results of 0.04 or higher;</li>
                            <li>Verified positive drug tests;</li>
                            <li>Refusals to be tested (including adulterated or substituted samples);</li>
                            <li>Other DOT drug and alcohol violations;</li>
                            <li>Rule violations reported by prior employers;</li>
                            <li>Documentation of completed return-to-duty processes.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </p>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        Additionally, I authorize release of:
                        <ul>
                            <li>Dates and names of previous employers;</li>
                            <li>Reasons for employment termination;</li>
                            <li>Work experience and accidents;</li>
                            <li>Academic history and professional credentials.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </p>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        I also authorize the release of records showing negative test results or results below 0.04, and the contact details of any substance abuse professionals who evaluated me during the three-year period.
                    </p>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        Consumer reports may also be obtained from HireRight and DriverFacts containing public records (e.g., driving record, workers' compensation claims, criminal history, etc.), previous employment data, policy violations, or drug/alcohol use history.
                    </p>
                    <h6 class="mt-3 mb-1">PSP Disclosure and Authorization (FMCSA)</h6>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        In connection with my application for employment, the Prospective Employer and its authorized agents may obtain one or more reports regarding my commercial driving and safety inspection history through the FMCSA's Pre-Employment Screening Program (PSP).
                    </p>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        If applying in person and if any adverse employment decision is based on PSP data, the Prospective Employer will provide me with a copy of the report and a summary of my rights under the Fair Credit Reporting Act prior to taking any final action.
                    </p>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        If I apply via mail, phone, or electronically, and if adverse action is taken based on PSP data, the Prospective Employer will notify me within three business days, including:
                        <ul>
                            <li>That adverse action has been taken based in whole or in part on FMCSA information;</li>
                            <li>FMCSA's name, address, and toll-free phone number;</li>
                            <li>Notice that FMCSA did not make the decision and cannot explain the reason for the action;</li>
                            <li>My right to request a copy of the report and dispute inaccuracies.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </p>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        I understand that FMCSA cannot correct crash or inspection data; such requests must be submitted to <a href="https://dataqs.fmcsa.dot.gov" target="_blank">https://dataqs.fmcsa.dot.gov</a>, and will be forwarded to the appropriate State for review.
                    </p>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        The PSP report includes all Commercial Motor Vehicle (CMV) crashes and inspections reported to FMCSA, regardless of fault, and includes violations adjudicated by a court.
                        I understand and acknowledge that this information may be used by the Prospective Employer to determine my suitability for employment.
                    </p>
                    <p class="my-2">
                        By signing or electronically accepting this agreement, I authorize the Prospective Employer and its agents to access my PSP report and related safety performance information.
                    </p>
                </section>
                <div class="row mt-3">
                    <div class="col-md-9 text-start mb-2">
                        <div class="form-check">
                            <input type="checkbox" class="form-check-input" id="agree" disabled />
                            <label class="form-check-label" for="agree" style="font-size: .82em;">
                                I agree and accept the Terms and Conditions
                            </label>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-3">
                        <form id="apl-submit-form" action="{{actionUrl.submit}}" method="POST">
                            <div class="d-grid">
                                <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary bg-primary-subtle btn-sm" id="apl-submit" disabled>Submit</button>
                            </div>
                        </form>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card-footer text-secondary">
                {{{copyright}}}
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>
    <script type="module" src="/modules/application/agreement.mjs"></script>

{{> foot}}